{"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/bipartiteEdgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/chromaticNumber()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(order:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyEdgeColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEdgeColoring(_:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isVertexColoring(_:)","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumColoring()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Extended Protocol","title":"Graph","externalID":"s:e:s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE04edgeC0AD04EdgeC0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"extension","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/bipartiteEdgeColoring()":{"title":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bipartiteEdgeColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","text":"EdgeColoring","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/bipartiteEdgeColoring()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/bipartiteedgecoloring()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with exactly Δ colours, Δ counting parallel edges, on a bipartite graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(König’s theorem), or nil when the graph is not bipartite ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"findOddCycle()"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"witness; a self-loop makes it not bipartite). Parallel edges are fine. Edges in position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order: each takes the least colour free at its end with the lesser vertex index, after the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternating path of that colour and the least colour free at the other end is flipped from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the other end, when the two differ there. O(m · (n + Δ)) time, O(n + m) memory."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/chromaticNumber()":{"abstract":[{"text":"The chromatic number χ of the simple graph (self-loops ignored, parallel edges once): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fewest colours of a proper colouring. 0 for the empty graph, 1 without edges, 2 when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite with an edge (BipartiteGraphs’ two-colouring, O(n + m)). Otherwise the greatest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the connected components, each non-bipartite one decided by DSatur branch and bound","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Brélaz 1979) between a greedy clique and greedy DSatur. Exponential in the worst case:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mycielski graphs, whose χ exceeds ω by a lot, are the hard ones. The search does not check","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"chromaticNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/chromaticNumber()","title":"chromaticNumber()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/chromaticnumber()"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(strategy:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","abstract":[{"text":"A greedy colouring of the simple graph (self-loops ignored, parallel edges once): each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in the strategy’s order takes the least colour none of its already coloured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbours has. Colours are first-fit numbers, not renumbered: colour 0 goes to the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex coloured. At most Δ + 1 colours (","type":"text"},{"code":".smallestLast","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": degeneracy + 1). O(n + m) for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"largest first and connected sequential, O((n + m) log n) for smallest last, DSatur and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colored neighbours, O(χ (n + m) log n) for independent set.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(strategy:)"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyEdgeColoring()":{"title":"greedyEdgeColoring()","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedyedgecoloring()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A greedy edge colouring of any graph, parallel edges and self-loops included, with at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2Δ − 1 colours: the largest-first colouring of the line graph. Edges by the number of other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges they share an end with, most first (a parallel copy counts at both ends, a self-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"meets each other edge at its vertex once), ties in position order; each takes the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour of no edge it shares an end with that is already coloured. A self-loop is one edge at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its vertex, as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isEdgeColoring(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n + m · Δ) time, O(n + m) memory, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"building the line graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyEdgeColoring()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyEdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/isEdgeColoring(_:)":{"title":"isEdgeColoring(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isEdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isEdgeColoring(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isedgecoloring(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Whether every two edges with a common end have different colours: parallel edges, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share both ends, and a self-loop and any other edge at its vertex. Any Ints count as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours. ","type":"text"},{"code":"color","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per edge, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. O(n + m), plus one hash per edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the colours are not small non-negative numbers.","type":"text"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/edgeColoring()":{"title":"edgeColoring()","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"type":"text","text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule04EdgeA0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EdgeColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumColoring()":{"title":"minimumColoring()","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcoloring()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An optimal colouring of the simple graph: ","type":"text"},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with colours","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numbered by first appearance in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order (the first vertex has colour 0, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour first appears after the one below it). It is the colouring ","type":"text"},{"code":"chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search finds, so it costs the same: a bipartite graph gets its ","type":"text"},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sides (left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0), and each other component the colouring that DSatur branch and bound found for it, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"greedy DSatur’s when that already uses no more colours than another component needs.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Deterministic, but which optimal colouring it is depends on the search; for one fixed by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rule, see ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Exponential in the worst case, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is; the search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumColoring()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(order:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"First fit in "},{"code":"order","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the simple graph: each vertex in turn takes the least colour none of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its already coloured neighbours has. A shuffled "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a random sequential"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colouring. At most Δ + 1 colours. O(n + m) after one lookup per vertex."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"greedyColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"order","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(order:)","title":"greedyColoring(order:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(order:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The greedy colouring with some colours fixed in advance: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presetColor"},{"text":" gives a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colour, or nil to leave it to the strategy. Preset vertices keep their colours and count as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coloured from the start; the others are coloured as by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"text":", each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"taking the least colour no coloured neighbour has. The orders of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".largestFirst"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".smallestLast"},{"text":" and the connected sequential strategies are those of the whole graph with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the preset vertices skipped (whole-graph degrees); DSatur counts preset colours in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saturation from the start; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".independentSet"},{"text":"‘s class k starts without the neighbours of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices preset to k; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"text":" counts preset neighbours as coloured and takes its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first vertex from its heap. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount"},{"text":" is one more than the greatest colour, so preset","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"colours may leave some colours unused. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presetColor"},{"text":" is called once per vertex, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. The strategy’s time, plus O(n + m) to check the presets.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"greedyColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO","text":"ColoringStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"presetColor"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","title":"greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/greedycoloring(strategy:presetcolor:)"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Coloring","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/isVertexColoring(_:)":{"title":"isVertexColoring(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isVertexColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isVertexColoring(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isvertexcoloring(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"color"},{"text":" gives the two ends of every edge different colours. Self-loops are ignored,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the colourings ignore them. Any Ints count as colours, not only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<k"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"color"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per vertex, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. O(n + m)."}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","role":"collection"}}}